  "correctness": "All reference decisions match. Native router maximum raw-logit error 0.00000525; native digit error 0.00003052 in this initial revision. Separate repeated CPU/GPU fixture replay and vector-kernel tests pass.",
  "changes": "Cached rotary tables; last-layer first-query pruning; AVX2/FMA packed float32 projections, vector LayerNorm, vector erf-form GeGLU and softmax; bounded 64 MiB/128-buffer activation reuse. Native CPU keeps original uint8 embeddings. Non-x86 paths use the portable Rust GEMM and scalar fallbacks.",
  "qualification": "The router wins median and p99 on the mixed corpus at both thread budgets. At exactly 512 tokens its median is faster but p99 is worse in this initial matrix; neither engine meets the 20 ms CPU target. Digit inference matches ORT at one thread but trails at four in this initial matrix. Worker affinity and a subsequent digit revision are being qualified separately; these initial results remain visible.",
